meta {
  name: Get History
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/options/history/TSLA261016C00360000?count=200&timespan=M5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  count: 200
  timespan: M5
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Get Option Historical Bars

  Returns historical OHLCV bars for a single option contract (the options mirror
  of /api/history/{ticker}). Backed by the Webull v3 Data API endpoint
  GET /market-data/options/bars/list (category=US_OPTION).

  ## Path
  - `{occSymbol}` — the OCC option code, e.g. TSLA261016C00360000
    (= TSLA, exp 2026-10-16, CALL, strike 360). You can get valid OCC codes from
    the "Get Contracts" response after loading.

  ## Query
  - `count`    — number of bars (default = app.options.bar-count; option max 1200).
  - `timespan` — bar granularity (default M5). Native only: M1, M5, M15, M30, M60,
    M120, M240, D, W, M, Y (no synthetic M2/M3 for options).

  ## Responses
  - `200` — { optionSymbol, timespan, count, bars: [ {timestamp, timestampEt, open,
             high, low, close, volume} ] }
  - `400` — invalid timespan
  - `502` — Webull error (includes `webullError`); e.g. 403 if US_OPTION is not subscribed
}
